			"module_doc": {
				"doc": "Extract stylesheet dependencies and feature evidence through a CSS parser. A regular expression cannot reliably distinguish a URL token from a quoted string, a comment or a nested rule.\n\nExtract URL references first, then collect custom properties, media features and pseudo classes from the same parsed stylesheet. References retain source positions for diagnostics. Resolve relative URLs against the stylesheet URL in your application. Parsing performs no network fetch and does not tell you whether a feature is supported by a particular browser.\n",
				"tags": [
					{
						"kind": "example",
						"doc": "```ts\nimport * as css from '@okikio/css';\nconst source = '@import \"theme.css\"; .hero { background: url(\"hero.webp\"); --accent: blue; }';\nconst parsed = css.parse(source);\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(css.resources(parsed).map((item) => item.url)));\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(css.customProperties(parsed)));\n```\n"
					},
					{
						"kind": "module"
					}
				]
			},
